WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.717
Here is one defensible e-commerce analysis direction.

00:00:02.717 --> 00:00:06.462
Device type is nominal and works naturally with one-hot encoding.

00:00:06.462 --> 00:00:10.297
Membership tier is ordinal when the business defines a real ranking.

00:00:10.297 --> 00:00:12.827
Session duration is a ratio measurement.

00:00:12.827 --> 00:00:15.542
Purchase count is a discrete ratio count.

00:00:15.542 --> 00:00:20.447
Weekday often behaves as a cyclical category because Sunday connects back to Monday.

00:00:20.447 --> 00:00:25.602
Revenue should use an exact numeric storage type, with currency documented separately.

00:00:25.602 --> 00:00:30.077
Connect this idea to a university analyzing student records, surveys, and learning-platform activity.

00:00:30.077 --> 00:00:35.322
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:35.322 --> 00:00:40.787
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:40.787 --> 00:00:45.182
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:45.182 --> 00:00:50.009
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
